# Hydrogen combustion: derive the balanced equation and certify it,
# exported as std.chem.balance + std.chem.mass_balance cells through
# the std::chemistry field pack (science lane rymw).
#
# balance(S): S is the SIGN-BLIND species composition matrix (rows =
# elements H, O; cols = species H2, O2, H2O; entry = atoms of the
# element in the species). The cell returns the canonical primitive
# coefficient vector [2, 1, -2] for 2 H2 + O2 -> 2 H2O (reactants
# positive, products negative).
#
# mass_balance(S, s): certifies a signed coefficient vector — the
# per-element residual S·s is EXACTLY zero for a balanced equation;
# otherwise it refuses typed MassImbalance(element i, residual r).
#
# The cell chain balance(S) then mass_balance(S, balance(S)) is the
# mass-conservation certificate. Both cells are registry DATA over
# generic nucleus ops (matvec, int_nullspace); no per-reaction code.
# Run: emath check language/examples/chemistry/combustion-mass-balance.emath
package std

emath field_pack chemistry:
    exports:
        cell balance
        cell mass_balance
    metadata:
        description hydrogen combustion balancing plus mass balance certificate
